<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahlamu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ahlamu were nomadic groups of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> named in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> sources from the 14th century BCE, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a> and Kassite letters from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a>. Assyrian kings fought them along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, and from the time of Tiglath-pileser I they were linked with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaeans">Aramaeans</a> as 'Ahlamu-Aramaeans', so the name came to stand for Aramaean nomads.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahlamu.jpg" alt="Ahlamu" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: yeowatzup · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syrian_Desert_(5079180729).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
